<title>SWITZERLAND: G10 SEES GOOD GROWTH IN US, CANADA.</title>
<headline>G10 SEES GOOD GROWTH IN US, CANADA.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said G10 central bank governors saw a positive outlook for growth without inflation in the United States and Canada.</p>
<p>Tietmeyer was speaking after the governors' monthly meeting at the Bank for International Settlements, which included a briefing from U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan and Bank of Canada Governor Gordon Thiessen.</p>
<p>&quot;I think both countries have all in all a relatively positive outlook as far as growth is concerned and as far as no inflationary growth is concerned,&quot; he told reporters. </p>
<p>Tietmeyer, chairman of the central bank governors' panel, did not elaborate.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
